summary:
I re-derived about 30 results in informal.tex, physics.tex and their appendices against T3 and T4, including every repair recorded in their Verification logs and the full Def 5.2 checklist. All proofs check line by line. The worked numbers reproduce from T3-checks: the sps_checker table, the thin-leg thresholds, the Monte Carlo bins, the projectile, small-angle, conformal and drag figures, and the realizability counts. T4-checks/run_all.sh also reproduces in full.

Two real gaps remain, both at the checker/theorem interface, and both were flagged as minor in round-2 re-verification but never propagated:
- M1: the well-posedness certificate ω_c may be supplied by the solver. With ω_c := ⊤, the paper's own rope counterexample is accepted, so "sound for every solver whatsoever" is false as literally stated.
- M2: the reading ρ, including Ax_ρ, comes from the solver and is never checked. So the judgment layer is not "exactly" (J1)–(J3).

One cross-section overclaim survives the concurrent edits: intro.tex line 79 says mis-designation forces a "globally paraconsistent logic", but the proposition proves global sub-classicality.

The rest is minor:
- an imprecise hypothesis in Thm nofree(c);
- loose quantifiers in Thm judgment(b);
- an incomplete partial-support statement in Thm frz(iv), whose V2 check tests a condition the theorem never states (I verified a corrected rule on 160 cases);
- overclaims in Thm robust(d2) and Prop emergence(c);
- V7's "true error 0.159" does not reproduce (I get 0.150);
- leg_exact.py still prints superseded thresholds;
- brute-force counts need non-default script arguments;
- small wording and reference issues.

Full report: /home/user/AI-works/inferential-learning/research/paper-review/math-applied.md

